+# Philosophy
+
+For whoever proposes a new service or weighs how much the volunteers can operate. This page gives the rule for
+accepting that operational work. Written after [issue 70](../notes/issue-70.md) reopened the same argument over
+Elasticsearch for pantry item search, and the team asked that the next proposal start from the rule.
+
+## Tenets
+
+### Prefer the services the volunteers already operate.
+
+A proposal to add a service the volunteers would operate must show both something Postgres cannot do and two
+volunteers able to restore the new service. This rules out adding a service just because someone can set it up:
+the team must be able to run it when that person is away. Start a proposal with those two conditions.
+
+In issue 70, searching for "rice" took four seconds and missed "Rice, brown". Elasticsearch was proposed, but
+Postgres full-text search on the item name brought it to 40 ms and found the missing item. The proposer chose
+Postgres instead.
+
+The rule allows external services such as the card gateway and hosted services that nobody on the team has to
+operate; it is not a ban on services outside Postgres.
+
+Applied in [keeping sessions in the database](adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md) and
+[running background jobs on Postgres](adrs/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md).
